      "text": "We will classify the range by considering cases for $x \\geq 1$, $-1 \\le x < 1$, and $x \\le -1$.\nCase 1: $x \\ge 1$\nIn this case, $x+1 \\ge 2$ and $|x-1| = x-1$. Thus, $$G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = (x+1) - (x-1) = 2.$$\nCase 2: $-1 \\le x < 1$\nIn this case, $|x+1| = x+1$ and $|x-1| = 1-x$. Thus, $$G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = (x+1) - (1-x) = 2x.$$\nSince $-1 \\le x < 1$, $0 \\le 2x < 2$, so the range for this case is $[0,2)$.\nCase 3: $x \\le -1$\nIn this case, $x+1 \\le 0$, and $|x-1| = -x+1$. Thus, $$G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| = -(x+1) - (-x+1) = -2.$$\nIn conclusion, the range of the function $G(x)$ is $\\boxed{(-\\infty,-2) \\cup [0,2)}$.The answer is: (-\\infty,-2)\\cup[0,2)",
