    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to analyze the expression step by step, considering different cases based on the value of \\( x \\).\n\n### Case 1: \\( x \\geq 1 \\)\nFor \\( x \\geq 1 \\), both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are non-negative. Therefore, the absolute values can be removed without change:\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x + 1 - x + 1 = 2\n\\]\nSo, for \\( x \\geq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n\n### Case 2: \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\)\nFor \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\), \\( x+1 \\) is non-negative and \\( x-1 \\) is negative. Therefore, we need to consider the expression in two parts:\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (-(x-1)) = x + 1 + x - 1 = 2x\n\\]\nSo, for \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\). Since \\( x \\) ranges from \\(-1\\) to \\(1\\) (exclusive), \\( 2x \\) ranges from \\(-2\\) to \\(2\\) (exclusive).\n\n### Case 3: \\( x < -1 \\)\nFor \\( x < -1 \\), both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are negative. Therefore, we need to consider the expression in two parts:\n\\[\nG(x) = -(x+1) - (-(x-1)) = -x - 1 + x - 1 = -2\n\\]\nSo, for \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n\n### Combining the Results\nFrom the above cases, we have:\n- For \\( x \\geq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n- For \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\), and the range is \\([-2, 2)\\).\n- For \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n\nThe minimum value of \\( G(x) \\) is \\(-2\\) (from the case \\( x < -1 \\)), and the maximum value is \\(2\\) (from the case \\( x \\geq 1 \\)). The function \\( G(x) \\) is continuous and takes on all values between \\(-2\\) and \\(2\\) inclusive.\n\nTherefore, the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\) is \\([-2, 2]\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\n\\]",
